{
  "id": "Compound::DB01241 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Gemfibrozil is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions that involve both receptor activation and enzyme participation. The evidence suggests that Gemfibrozil, through its inclusion in PPAR-alpha agonists and its relationship with Fenofibrate, binds to Cyp3a4. This binding is supported by the lowest common ancestor analysis, which identifies a shared pathway involving aromatic ethers and fibrate antilipidemic agents. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism where Gemfibrozil, as an agonist of PPAR-alpha, indirectly influences Cyp3a4 by activating a metabolic enzyme involved in lipid metabolism. The evidence also indicates that Gemfibrozil directly interacts with Cyp2c9, which in turn participates in the oxidation of quinones and similar compounds, a process that is also associated with Cyp3a4. This suggests a broader metabolic pathway where Gemfibrozil may influence Cyp3a4 through multiple, interconnected mechanisms, emphasizing the role of enzyme participation in drug action.",
